T = {
    "897": "CHAPTER 7\n\nRecommendations and Directions for Future Research",

    "898": "7.1. Theoretical Implications: A Processual Re-conceptualization of Seizing",

    "899": "This study takes as its point of departure the empirical observation that judgments formed within organizations following AI utilization training requests do not necessarily convert into strategic decisions. It has demonstrated that such conversion failures are neither coincidental occurrences nor attributable to individual competency deficiencies, but are deeply intertwined with the alignment of processual conditions and institutional initiation structures required for the activation of Seizing within Dynamic Capabilities Theory. Accordingly, this section advances several theoretical recommendations for the existing Seizing framework based on the research findings.",

    "900": "First, this study strongly urges a comprehensive re-conceptualization of the Seizing phase through a thoroughly processual lens, decisively departing from the prevailing scholarly inertia that has treated it as a momentary, single-instance act of decision-making. Upon meticulous examination of the empirical trajectory, the organizational system successfully arrived at generating normative internal judgments by recognizing environmental turbulence and technological opportunities from the external ecosystem; however, at the critical juncture where such judgments were to leap onto the stage of formal decision-making, a fatal structural disconnection was observed. This unequivocally demonstrates that Seizing is by no means a fragmentary capability manifested solely at the specific moment a choice is made, but must be expanded into a concept encompassing the entire continuous trajectory from the inception of a judgment to its institutional incorporation within the organization\u2019s formal institutional apparatus. The logical conclusion is, therefore, that the essence of this phase must be reformulated not around the ex post presence or absence of \u2018decision output,\u2019 but around how \u2018minimum procedural initiation conditions\u2019\u2014such as the explicit designation of authorized responsible agents, the elevation of agenda items to formal deliberative bodies, and the coordination of concrete implementation timelines\u2014are interlocked and activated.",

    "901": "Second, this study exposes through empirical evidence that the frustration of the Seizing phase does not necessarily manifest as overt rejection of the matter at hand or as visible conflict among organizational members. The stagnation observed within the ecosystem under investigation more closely resembled a tenacious morass of non-decision\u2014wherein no substantive decision was gestated at all, rather than a specific \u2018failure of decision.\u2019 This insight provides compelling justification for elevating the so-called \u2018evaporated state of decision\u2019\u2014a phenomenon that prior Dynamic Capabilities research had thoroughly marginalized\u2014to the most critical object of anatomical inquiry within Seizing theory. In other words, the superficial approach of adjudicating the actual activation of this mechanism solely by the presence or absence of a final output must be abandoned, and the structural conditions under which the vacuum state that suppresses the gestation of any complete decision is incessantly varied and reproduced must be rigorously explicated in the language of theory.",

    "902": "Third, this inquiry draws a clear demarcation against existing micro-level approaches that have sought to reduce the substance of Seizing capability to the fragmented cognitive abilities of individual practitioners or the charismatic attributes of leaders. Upon examining the empirical trajectory, awareness regarding the necessity of adoption had already matured sufficiently at the level of individual members\u2019 professional expertise; nonetheless, in a vacuum where institutional mediating devices and procedural triggers capable of channeling this into formal organizational decisions had evaporated, the Seizing mechanism fell thoroughly silent. This maximally amplifies the necessity of repositioning the Seizing phase of Dynamic Capabilities not as mere \u2018individual-level cognitive agility\u2019 but as \u2018organizational-level processual capability\u2019 that is meticulously designed and structured within the macro-level system. Ultimately, Seizing must be evaluated not as a product forged by the resolution of specific heroic individuals, but as the outcome of the vigorous collective operation of pluralistic structural conditions constructed to enable the organizational ecosystem to fully absorb gestated judgments and translate them into the language of substantive decision-making.",

    "903": "Fourth, this study proposes a processual re-examination of the assumption of linear sequential linkage among Sensing\u2013Seizing\u2013Transforming within Dynamic Capabilities Theory. As the case demonstrated, although Sensing and judgment formation were achieved, the process stagnated at the Seizing stage, and the transition to Transforming was never initiated. This suggests that the stages of Dynamic Capabilities do not automatically cascade in sequence, but that each stage harbors distinct operating conditions and possibilities of failure. Accordingly, Seizing needs to be more precisely theorized not as a mere intermediate stage, but as a processual bottleneck that determines the success or failure of the entire Dynamic Capabilities framework.",

    "904": "In sum, this study theoretically recommends that Dynamic Capabilities Theory be supplemented with processual depth by redefining Seizing not as a \u2018moment of decision\u2019 but as the entire process through which judgments are incorporated\u2014or fail to be incorporated\u2014into the organization\u2019s decision-making structure. Such re-conceptualization will provide a theoretical foundation enabling future Seizing research to explain a broader range of empirical phenomena, encompassing not only successful cases but also organizational states in which decisions do not occur.",

    "905": "7.2. Practical Implications: Organizational Design Principles for the Judgment\u2013Decision Transition after AI Utilization Training Requests",

    "906": "This study departed from the unequivocal empirical observation that normative judgments gestated within organizational ecosystems following AI utilization training requests never automatically leap onto the stage of strategic decision-making. The multilayered case analysis revealed that such an intransigent conversion gap cannot be reduced to incidental administrative omissions or competency deficits of specific operational staff. Rather, it is intimately connected to a structural blind spot wherein the \u2018processual configuration\u2019 and \u2018institutional initiation structure\u2019 that must be presupposed for the actual activation of the Seizing phase posited by Dynamic Capabilities Theory had not been fully constructed within the organization. Accordingly, this section proposes the practical direction in which organizational design at the field level should be comprehensively reformed, grounded in the preceding empirical findings, so that AI utilization training requests may transcend mere transient learning and leap toward substantive outcomes.",

    "907": "First, the internal decision-making system of the organization must be comprehensively redesigned to mandate \u2018minimum procedural initiation conditions\u2019 capable of channeling gestated judgments onto the institutional track, departing from the inertia of fixating solely on ex post \u2018decision output.\u2019 Examination of the empirical trajectory reveals that, despite organizational members\u2019 awareness of environmental turbulence and new technological opportunities having matured to the point of producing firmly established judgments, no follow-up procedure existed to propel these forward, thereby inducing severe stagnation. This suggests that, to substantively realize Seizing capability in practice, a \u2018procedural calling system\u2019\u2014which, immediately upon the anchoring of a judgment, designates authorized responsible agents without delay, elevates agenda items to formal deliberative bodies, and assigns concrete implementation timelines\u2014must be enforced as the paramount principle of organizational design.",

    "908": "Second, institutional monitoring mechanisms capable of preemptively detecting and defending against the vacuum state of so-called \u2018non-decision,\u2019 which evaporates silently without any explicit resistance, must be urgently established. As this case starkly exposes, the frustration of conversion does not surface in the form of overt opposition or official rejection decisions; rather, it manifests as a condition in which the next procedure simply fails to open, left abandoned in profound silence. From a practical standpoint, therefore, the operational status of Seizing must not be adjudicated solely by the existence of a final decision document. The organizational system must recognize the terrain of \u2018un-decided-ness\u2019\u2014wherein a given matter is neither rejected nor approved but left adrift\u2014as a critical organizational risk signal, and must meticulously design an institutional safety net that mandatorily recalls agenda items that have remained pending beyond a designated period or records explicit grounds for their formal abandonment.",

    "909": "Third, the \u2018person-dependent\u2019 approach that relies on the charisma of individual leaders or the cognitive agility of members to drive the transition from judgment to full-fledged decision-making must be thoroughly abandoned, and this capacity must instead be firmly structured as a \u2018processual capability\u2019 guaranteed at the systemic level. In the ecosystem under investigation, normative judgments at the operational staff level had already sufficiently matured; yet the Seizing mechanism fell thoroughly silent because the institutional trigger required to launch these into the broader decision-making network had collapsed. In other words, practical Seizing capability in the field is not governed by the decisiveness of outstanding heroic individuals, but must be comprehensively reformed into a \u2018vigorously collective operational apparatus of pluralistic structural conditions\u2019 in which the organizational ecosystem is obligated to absorb gestated judgments and translate them into the language of formal decision-making.",

    "910": "Fourth, the performance evaluation metrics at the organizational level must be comprehensively reformed to center on \u2018institutional incorporation\u2019\u2014whether gestated judgments have been safely anchored onto the track of formal institutional procedures\u2014rather than on the fragmented learning outcomes of individuals. The myopic approach that, following prevailing inertia, seeks to measure the outcomes generated by AI utilization training requests solely through participants\u2019 subjective satisfaction or marginal improvements in technical proficiency can never three-dimensionally capture whether the organization\u2019s most critical judgment\u2013decision-making conversion mechanism has actually awakened.",

    "911": "When viewed through the structural lens of this inquiry, genuine performance must be rigorously determined by whether normative judgments constructed within the organizational system have successfully entered the substantive decision-making network. In other words, the firm practical conclusion is reached that, rather than treating mere training completion rates as the final destination, the very fact of whether judgments \u2018have leaped into the institutional decision-making structure\u2019\u2014through the explicit designation of authorized responsible agents, the elevation of agenda items to formal deliberative bodies, and the coordination of concrete implementation timelines\u2014must be firmly established as the most critical Key Performance Indicator driving the organization.",

    "912": "7.3. Policy and Institutional Recommendations: Institutional Mechanisms for Enabling the Judgment\u2013Decision Transition",

    "913": "The case examined in this study demonstrates that when organizational-level judgments formed after AI utilization training requests are left to the discretion of individual departments or personnel, a state in which no decision occurs whatsoever may persist\u2014even in the absence of explicit opposition or official rejection. This suggests that the failure of the judgment\u2013decision transition may be interpreted as a structural phenomenon linked to the conditions of policy and institutional design, extending beyond problems of internal organizational operations. Accordingly, this section discusses policy and institutional conditions that may be considered in the process of converting judgments into organizational-level decisions following AI utilization training requests, based on the research findings.",

    "914": "First, AI utilization training needs to be understood at the policy level not merely as an \u2018educational program,\u2019 but as an institutional event capable of exerting influence on the organization\u2019s formal decision-making system. In the case organization, AI training was recognized as a capacity-building activity; however, the policy conditions under which its outcomes should be linked to organizational-level decision-making agendas were not clearly established. As a result, judgments generated after training remained at the level of reference information. This suggests that, depending on what institutional status AI utilization training requests are accorded, the subsequent trajectory of judgments may differ.",

    "915": "Second, this study demonstrates that the existence of formal review procedures for handling post-training judgments significantly influences the judgment\u2013decision transition. In the case organization, no formal deliberative body or procedure was clearly designated to review post-training judgments or to determine whether decision-making should proceed. Consequently, judgments could not be attributed to the responsibility of any specific body, and as a result, they failed to enter the decision-making agenda. This suggests that, at the policy level, the designation of formal procedures to receive judgments constitutes a structural condition that governs the possibility of decision initiation.",

    "916": "Third, in order to facilitate the conversion of judgments, institutional review of how the state of decision deferral is managed is required. In this case, judgments were deferred for extended periods without explicit opposition, and throughout this process, the responsible agents and timelines gradually became unclear. This may be interpreted as a phenomenon arising from the absence of criteria regarding how long judgments can be institutionally maintained. Therefore, at the level of policy and institutional design, it is necessary to include management mechanisms that explicitly stipulate the conditions under which the deferred status of judgments formed after AI utilization training requests persists or terminates. In this regard, even for matters classified as Soft Trigger applications as proposed earlier, a Time-lagged Escalation policy must be institutionally stipulated whereby, should a specific pending period (e.g., three or six months) be exceeded, the matter automatically converts to a Hard Trigger and is mandatorily placed on the agenda as either a formal abandonment or implementation proposal.",

    "917": "Fourth, this study suggests that the institutional identifiability of responsible agents\u2014that is, accountability visibility\u2014is critical for connecting judgments related to AI utilization training requests to the organizational decision-making structure. In the case organization, regardless of the validity of the judgment, the authority and responsibility for advancing it to the next stage were not institutionally specified. This demonstrates that such a condition may function as a structural factor that confines judgments to the level of individual perceptions or informal discussions. From a policy perspective, how the roles of managing, coordinating, and placing judgments on formal agendas are institutionally arranged may be understood as one of the core conditions for the judgment\u2013decision transition.",

    "918": "Finally, this study raises the necessity of including within policy and institutional design not only \u2018the outcomes of decisions\u2019 but also \u2018the state in which decisions have not occurred\u2019 as an object of analysis. Organizations can inspect not only what decisions were made after AI utilization training requests, but also record and review why judgments were not converted into decisions and at which stage they stagnated. Such an approach may lead to the construction of an institutional feedback mechanism aimed at learning from the structural vulnerabilities of the judgment\u2013decision conversion mechanism.",

    "919": "In sum, the policy and institutional recommendations of this study focus not on reducing the phenomenon whereby judgments \u2018remained undecided despite their existence\u2019 after AI utilization training requests to individual passivity or organizational culture, but rather on analytically examining how such states emerge and are sustained within the design conditions of policy and institutions. From this perspective, this study presents analytical criteria and design principles for identifying the institutional conditions that enable the judgment\u2013decision transition after AI utilization training requests.",

    "921": "7.4. Methodological Recommendations: Studying Non-Events and Process Breakdowns",

    "922": "The multilayered case analysis of this inquiry clearly demonstrates that when judgments gestated within the organizational system following AI utilization training requests are entrusted solely to the fragmented discretion of individual departments or operational staff and fail to ascend onto the institutional track, a vacuum state in which no genuine policy decision is gestated whatsoever may become permanently entrenched\u2014even in the complete absence of overt resistance or rejection. This strongly suggests that the fatal disconnection between judgment and decision cannot be dismissed as a transient administrative delay at the operational level, but must be interpreted as an intransigent structural product linked to blind spots in macro-level policy and institutional design. Drawing upon these empirical insights as a robust foundation, this section systematically formulates the essential policy and institutional prerequisites that must be satisfied for gestated judgments to cross the threshold of formal decision-making, as well as novel methodological orientations for capturing these phenomena.",

    "923": "First, future follow-up studies must decisively abandon the prevailing inertial approach of fixating exclusively on ex post visible events and instead adopt an innovative research design that elevates so-called \u2018non-events\u2019 themselves to the status of explicit units of analysis. The existing organizational research landscape has predominantly collected and analyzed empirical data by pursuing only the moments at which decisions were reached, specific points at which implementation was launched, or observable results produced. However, this inquiry has unequivocally demonstrated that, despite the firm existence of normative judgments, a \u2018state in which no procedural event whatsoever is gestated\u2019\u2014including non-placement on formal deliberative agendas, non-assignment of responsible agents, and non-establishment of implementation deadlines\u2014can be maintained in a highly structured manner within the organizational depths. The logical conclusion is, therefore, that future scholarly endeavors must not merely ask \u2018what has occurred\u2019 but must, from the very inception of research design, meticulously forge the criteria by which to document and explicate \u2018which essential procedures fell structurally silent after the AI utilization training request.\u2019",

    "924": "Second, it is revealed that \u2018institutional clarity\u2019\u2014concerning which formal procedures within the organizational system will fully absorb and verify gestated judgments\u2014functions as the most critical bifurcation point governing the transition between judgment and decision. Within the ecosystem under investigation, after the AI utilization training request was gestated, no dedicated deliberative body or institutional transit pathway for formally analyzing and resolving it had been constructed in the first place. As an inevitable consequence, the agenda remained adrift, unable to be incorporated into the official responsibility network of any department within the organization. In such a fragmented structure, no matter how robust the existing judgment may be, the institutional launch channel for propelling it onto the stage of complete decision-making is fundamentally sealed off. In other words, the evaporation of the formal vessel (pathway) to receive formed judgments itself functions as the most formidable structural barrier blocking the gestation of substantive decisions.",

    "925": "Third, to overcome the intransigent stagnation of the conversion phase, the establishment of institutional management criteria for rigorously controlling the \u2018decision deferral state\u2019 in which agenda items remain adrift is urgently required. The matter captured in the field was subjected to prolonged suspension amid profound silence despite the complete absence of overt opposition or conflict among members, and throughout this process, the originally gestated accountability and implementation timelines ultimately evaporated. This is an inevitable product of a vacuum state devoid of any minimum institutional deadline governing how long a raised judgment may sustain its viability as a formal policy agenda. Therefore, at the level of macro-level system design, a structural surveillance mechanism must be implanted that explicitly codifies under what conditions judgments accompanying AI utilization training requests have their validity extended or are finally rejected.",

    "926": "Fourth, as the most decisive prerequisite for channeling constructed judgments into the very center of the broader decision-making network, \u2018accountability visibility\u2019\u2014the institutional identifiability of responsible agents\u2014is strongly proposed. Upon meticulous examination of the subject case, entirely irrespective of the intrinsic validity possessed by the judgment, the clear authority and accountability for propelling it onto the trajectory of subsequent procedures were never articulated in the organizational language. A terrain in which the attribution of accountability has evaporated functions as the most fatal blind spot, degrading grand discourse into nothing more than fragmented perceptions of operational staff or informal tabletop deliberations. Viewed from a policy perspective, the conclusion converges upon the proposition that whether and how the agents of authority for actively grasping, coordinating, and elevating gestated agendas to formal deliberative bodies are positioned within the institutional network constitutes the absolute criterion governing the success or failure of the judgment\u2013decision transition.",

    "927": "Finally, this inquiry urges future macro-level system design to depart from the inertia of blindly fixating on ex post \u2018decision outputs\u2019 and instead subsume within precision analysis the very \u2018vacuum state in which decisions were not gestated\u2019 as a target of inquiry. Rather than retroactively adjudicating only the final outcomes produced subsequent to the AI utilization training request, the organizational ecosystem must meticulously record and reflect upon why robust judgments failed to cross the threshold of decision-making and at precisely which procedural juncture they became mired in stagnation. Such an innovative expansion of perspective will lead to the construction of a powerful institutional feedback mechanism for preemptively detecting and remedying the structural fissures of conversion mechanisms concealed within the organization.",

    "928": "In comprehensive assessment, the most weighty scholarly orientation of the methodological and policy recommendations forged in this section lies in thoroughly excluding the superficial attempt to reduce the disconnection phenomenon\u2014wherein clearly gestated judgments are ultimately submerged in the morass of non-decision\u2014to the passive attitudes of specific practitioners or to abstract organizational culture. Instead, the analytical focus is placed on rigorously dissecting through a structural lens how such intransigent stagnation acquires its own independent vitality and is tenaciously reproduced within the depths of macro-level institutional design and policy conditions. Upon these insights, this inquiry furnishes the academic community and the field with the sharpest analytical criteria and design archetypes for identifying the essential institutional prerequisites that the organizational system must construct to propel normative judgments formed after AI utilization training requests toward substantive decisions.",
}

